QNX: package the onnxruntime Python module

setup.py picks the compiled files to package by platform.system(). On QNX that
returns "QNX", which falls into the Windows branch, so setup.py looks for
onnxruntime_pybind11_state.pyd, finds nothing and silently leaves the real
onnxruntime_pybind11_state.so out of the package. `import onnxruntime` then
fails with "No module named 'onnxruntime.capi.onnxruntime_pybind11_state'".
QNX shares the Linux layout, so treat it like Linux.


--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -361,7 +361,7 @@
 dl_libs = []
 libs = []
 
-if platform.system() == "Linux" or platform.system() == "AIX":
+if platform.system() in ("Linux", "AIX", "QNX"):
     libs = [
         "onnxruntime_pybind11_state.so",
         "libdnnl.so.2",
